title: PowerShell WMI Event Subscription via Cmdlet
id: 7b98513d-e6b4-4c64-ab32-5ab563c80a06
status: experimental
description: Detects creation of WMI permanent event subscriptions through PowerShell cmdlets (Set-WmiInstance/New-CimInstance for __EventFilter, CommandLineEventConsumer, __FilterToConsumerBinding), a fileless persistence technique.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1546/003/
logsource:
  product: windows
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'Set-WmiInstance'
      - 'New-CimInstance'
      - 'Register-WmiEvent'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '__EventFilter'
      - 'CommandLineEventConsumer'
      - 'FilterToConsumerBinding'
      - 'ActiveScriptEventConsumer'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - Image
  - ParentImage
falsepositives:
  - Monitoring agents registering consumers
level: high
tags:
  - attack.persistence
  - attack.t1546.003
